WEBVTT

00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:18,220
In my blood test, the NK cells are 228, the range is 70-760.

00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,720
When the number is closer to the higher range,

00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:24,220
does that mean the immune system is better

00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:29,220
or it is fighting something or some kind of infection?

00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:31,220
That is why the number is higher,

00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:36,220
save with a CD3 to CD16 ratio.

00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:39,220
Yes, so when you look at...

00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:45,220
That is the problem when you look at a differentiation.

00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:49,220
Usually if you do CBC with a differential,

00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:52,220
it is only going to measure neutrophils.

00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:55,220
The differential is breaking down to the white blood cells

00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:58,220
and lymphocytes, neutrophils, monocytes, blah, blah, blah.

00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:02,220
It is not going to break it down deeper into NK cells,

00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:04,220
which are natural killer cells.

00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:09,220
And all the other CD cell line,

00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:11,220
unless you do a deep dive in it.

00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:14,220
There is argument whether the deep dive

00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,220
with a value of the deep dive.

00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:21,220
I don't recommend it even though one of the best tests for that

00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,220
is a Syrex.

00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:25,220
I forgot what it is, Ray 23.

00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,220
I think it is.

00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:28,220
That does the deep dive into that.

00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:32,220
But that would really be for immune dysfunction patients.

00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,220
That would be autoimmune issues.

00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:39,220
Not really even beneficial for cancer patients.

00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:41,220
And the reason is that, yes,

00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:47,220
you can have elevated or suppressed immune function most likely

00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:52,220
due to either current infection or an autoimmune disorder.

00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:55,220
So having 220 ate, you're right in the middle.

00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,220
That's normal.

00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:59,220
It would only be, you know, you could take all the immune...

00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:02,220
You could take bottles of immune stimulating supplements

00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:05,220
and it's probably not going to increase your natural killer cells.

00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:09,220
Because your body has a balance of what it's trying to achieve.

00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,220
You can't artificially change that.

00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:14,220
Because you're fighting a disease.

00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:18,220
So you can support it so that your body can make.

00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,220
So it's not depressed so that it's not...

00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:24,220
So it's able to keep up the demand that your body's making.

00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:27,220
But you can't just take a whole bunch of immune stimulation

00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:30,220
and think that your white blood cell count is going to be...

00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:34,220
is going to be elevated by simply doing that.

00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:38,220
So no, it's usually because you're fighting something

00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:43,220
or it's maybe you could also be in a hyper response

00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:46,220
in an autoimmune situation.

00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:49,220
Or if it's suppressed, depressed,

00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:54,220
you could have a suppressed immune situation.

00:02:54,220 --> 00:03:00,220
Also, you can't forget that you have to correlate to any medication

00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,220
that you're taking.

00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:05,220
Because medication can affect your bone marrow in production

00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:08,220
of white blood cells as well.

